<title>UK: M&amp;S gives UK staff 4.5 percent pay rise.</title>
<headline>M&amp;S gives UK staff 4.5 percent pay rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marks and Spencer Plc said on Tuesday it had awarded its staff a 3.5 percent pay increase for 1997/98, plus a one percent merit rise, making 4.5 percent overall.</p>
<p>The company announced the pay increase shortly after publishing results for its 1996/97 financial year, where profits were up nearly 11 percent to 1.1 billion stg.</p>
<p>M&amp;S is adding about 1,700 staff this year in the UK, where it is expanding space and boosting service levels in its existing stores.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
